# Git LFS.
#
# Patterns, not paths: these files are regenerated wholesale by the scripts in
# calibration/, and a regenerated asset written back under a new name would
# otherwise silently land in git proper.
#
# Requires `git lfs install` once per clone. Without it the working tree gets
# ~130-byte pointer files instead of the real data, and pyhmmer/torch fail on
# a malformed file rather than a missing one -- so if a profile scan or the
# AcrNET checkpoint load fails on a fresh clone, check this first:
#     git lfs env && git lfs pull

# Profile HMMs. ta_families.hmm alone is 12 MB and is needed at run time.
*.hmm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Model checkpoints (AcrNET, 2.5 MB) — binary, and never diffed usefully.
*.ckpt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pth  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
